To retrieve only the IDs of the CNAME records for **sample.com** via the VirusTotal API, you can query the DNS records endpoint and filter for type `CNAME`.  
Here’s a concise example using `curl`:

```bash
curl -X GET \
     "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/dns_records?type=CNAME" \
     -H "x-apikey: YOUR_API_KEY"
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual key (e.g., `secret123`).  

The JSON response will look something like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "record_1",
      "attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "record_2",
      "attributes": { ... }
    }
  ]
}
```

Extract the `"id"` values (`record_1`, `record_2`, …) from each object in the `"data"` array; those are the related object IDs you requested.
